  "behavior": [
    "Admission compares decoded payload/account identities, requires exactly one current account record with matching decoded public identity, and publishes its stored name.",
    "The private snapshot binds stored address, label, local/mobile/external/hardware classification, mobile topic, account genesis/ecosystem and local public key/type. Malformed flags, duplicate identities, unsupported keys and watch-only records lacking an explicit external signer reject.",
    "A nonempty account-bound genesis hash must match extrinsic genesis. Empty genesis remains unbound; raw bytes do not claim chain binding.",
    "Current account/key context is rechecked after phishing, after unlock, and after signing or mobile return. Public key derivation, pair.address and addressRaw must all match the reviewed identity, including exact algorithm/public key continuity across unlock.",
    "Local and mobile-returned signatures are cryptographically checked against the private queued bytes before release. Mobile transport receives a detached payload so mutation cannot rewrite the reviewed intent.",
    "Local signer classes no longer independently route to a global mobile service. Routing belongs to the approval handler and its captured signer classification. Explicit external/hardware accounts cannot enter local signing."
  ],
